  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian assistance for earthquake victims in Peru</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This emergency project will support 10,000 families (5 persons per family) out of the 40,000 affected families living in the areas of Ca&#xf1;ete, Chincha, Ica and Pisco who were affected by the earthquake that hit Peru in August 2007. The project will last between 19 August 2007 until 18 May 2008. Cartias Peru will work to provide immediate relief through food, nutrition and access to clean water; re-building of shelter will be the focus of the first two months. Re-construction work will also focus on re-building educational infrastructure and providing psychological/counselling support for families. Local emergency committees will be established to improve local capacity for reconstruction and rehabilitation.</narrative>
  </description>
